# A name computed sent to `self` in a module or a base class lowers only
# its own file: reaching every includer's and subclass's methods was tried
# and lowered hundreds of rows no send reaches (DEC-666), so Host#plain and
# Sub#other stay clear.
# A block's parameter hides the method's local of its name (Panel), and a
# shape written under a condition leaves the name it may not replace
# (Socket), and so does one in a loop, a pattern match or a block (PumpA,
# PumpB, PumpC); an unknown value written under a condition over a shape
# leaves a name computed (PumpD): each is a name computed, not the shape.
# A name a send of a send hands on is a call of the method its receiver
# finds, from any file (Valve#relayed), not of another class's (Bystander),
# nor of a private one `public_send` cannot run (Valve#hidden).
# One the index records no symbol for, an operator or a string, lowers the
# method of its name from any file (Grid), or of an alias of it (Spout).
# A computed name sent to a constant in a Haml or ERB template names it
# (Gauge, Dial).
dead app Host#plain=unreferenced~ Sub#other=unreferenced~ Unrelated#lonely=unreferenced~ Panel#other_w=unreferenced~Panel Socket#other_g=unreferenced~Socket Valve#relayed=none Bystander#relayed=convention-only Valve#hidden=convention-only Grid#%=unreferenced~:% Grid#+=unreferenced~:+ Grid#spelled=unreferenced~spelled Grid#unsent=unreferenced~ Gauge#reading=unreferenced~Gauge Dial#reading=unreferenced~Dial Spout#pour=convention-only~tip PumpA#other=unreferenced~PumpA PumpB#other=unreferenced~PumpB PumpC#other=unreferenced~PumpC PumpD#other=unreferenced~PumpD
